1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,920
THIS SHOW IS CREATED
FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
THE CHARACTERS, BEHAVIORS
AND EVENTS ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,920
THEY ARE NOT INTENDED
TO DEFAME OR CAUSE DAMAGE

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,720
TO ANY ORGANIZATION OR INDIVIDUAL

5
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,400
‎VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED

6
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,400
You want a bigger piece of the pie?

7
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:31,680
Submit a proposal
to open the border for me.

8
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:39,840
Seehan's group has a meeting
at the youth training center.

9
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:43,480
<i>They will sign the papers</i>
<i>to launch the border project.</i>

10
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:46,360
Methee, shoot him.

11
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:51,880
<i>Finish him.</i>

12
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,760
<i>I received orders</i>
<i>to provide security here.</i>

13
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:45,720
What's up?

14
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:48,520
Sarawut is on duty here too.

15
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:51,160
They must have secured
the whole area by now.

16
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,640
What now?

17
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:58,280
No matter what,

18
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:02,800
I have to stop him
before he signs off on it.

19
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,840
How can I help?

20
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:14,000
If this document is approved,

21
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:18,040
our success is well within our reach.

22
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:23,880
So, let's celebrate
our success in advance.

23
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:28,000
Cheers.

24
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:31,840
Decha.

25
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,560
As soon as you sign this document,

26
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:38,040
we can submit it to the Cabinet.

27
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:41,400
Once it reaches the Cabinet, don't worry.

28
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:44,560
I've prepared everything,
both the capital and the personnel.

29
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:47,160
Everything is set.
All we need is your signature.

30
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:53,400
If this project is approved,

31
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:57,880
I'll expedite opening
the border crossing as fast as possible.

32
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:02,560
Travel and financial transactions

33
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:03,800
will be much faster.

34
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:07,680
I believe
success won't wait around for us.

35
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:09,240
So we need to hurry.

36
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:11,320
Hm. True that.

37
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:29,760
Hey.

38
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,640
You can't enter.

39
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:37,960
Excuse me. Mr. Decha
ordered a birthday cake.

40
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:42,640
Whose birthday?
Today isn't General Decha's birthday.

41
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,360
The team said

42
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:49,560
Mr. Decha ordered a surprise cake
for Ms. Sirin's birthday.

43
00:05:57,840 --> 00:05:58,880
Sir.

44
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:01,320
What's going on?

45
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:04,200
Did you order a birthday cake
to surprise Ms. Sirin?

46
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:08,200
I didn't order it.

47
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:19,880
BAAN KANCHANAPISEK

48
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,840
Hey!

49
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,120
Smart move.

50
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,080
Go ahead.

51
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,520
Protect the VIPs. Go!

52
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,600
What's going on?

53
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:26,920
Sir.

54
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:52,800
MEMORANDUM

55
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:55,400
Kids, run! Hurry!

56
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,680
‎TWENTY-FIFTH ANNIVERSARY
‎REINTEGRATING GOOD CITIZENS

57
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,480
Gun!

58
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:22,200
You go ahead. I'll distract him.

59
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:24,800
Go.

60
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:50,240
TWENTY-FIFTH ANNIVERSARY
REINTEGRATING GOOD CITIZENS

61
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:08,760
Contact local police.
Clear the area immediately.

62
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:10,280
Yes, sir.

63
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:23,080
Ma'am, you are the only one left

64
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:26,440
to finish our work now.

65
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,480
Hey. Hey.

66
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:15,640
Gun.

67
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:22,360
Hey.

68
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,480
-<i>Don't! Hey!</i>
-<i>Let me go.</i>

69
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:46,160
-<i>Please let me go.</i>
-<i>What are you doing?</i>

70
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,920
Requesting authorization.

71
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,320
BORDER AREA
NO ENTRY WITHOUT PERMISSION

72
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:54,480
Grandma!

73
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:06,600
Grandma!

74
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:04,640
Oh, Methee?

75
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:32,360
-Hey.
-You…

76
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:36,640
Disappointed, huh?

77
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:40,480
Thought a beautiful girl would kiss you?

78
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:45,440
Just get the hell out of here.

79
00:14:56,040 --> 00:14:59,400
If you kick me out,
where am I supposed to go?

80
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:02,080
We're both targets now.

81
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:05,240
Sorry, man.

82
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,000
It's fine.

83
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,760
Friends have to look out for each other.

84
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:15,440
I just can't stand
living like a dog on the run.

85
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:34,920
I set yours on the table.

86
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:37,000
Thank you.

87
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:44,200
I'll feed you. Come on.

88
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:47,680
Open your mouth.

89
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:53,640
I can eat it myself.

90
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:57,360
You're good at everything,
except being a patient.

91
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:59,480
Open your mouth.

92
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:13,080
Good job.

93
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:16,960
When you're this sweet,
you're easier to care for.

94
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,080
One more bite.

95
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,720
They're more careful now.

96
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,400
I want bullets

97
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:47,760
with a longer range
than the ones you've made.

98
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:51,160
How would I do that? This isn't America.
You want even more range?

99
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:52,960
You're exaggerating.

100
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:56,320
How disappointing.

101
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:01,840
In that case,
I'll get someone else to do it.

102
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,319
I know a guy.

103
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:10,240
-His stuff is seriously powerful.
-Who?

104
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:19,280
-Mr. Delu.
-Huh?

105
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:23,200
Good. Mr. Delu.

106
00:17:25,319 --> 00:17:26,520
Who's this Mr. Delu, bro?

107
00:17:26,599 --> 00:17:28,480
Hey, give me back my phone.

108
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:29,920
No, I'll do it.

109
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,400
Are you sure?

110
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:34,640
I don't go back on my word.
A deal's a deal.

111
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:39,200
By the way, who's Mr. Delu?

112
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:45,840
Are you guys messing with me?

113
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:47,320
Are you--

114
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,960
Thanks, kid.

115
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:56,080
It's you, Mr. Delu… sional.

116
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:57,920
Delusional?

117
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:01,640
Hey, I'm not delusional. You guys are!

118
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:09,920
The door was barely open, yet he
still managed to shoot General Decha.

119
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:10,880
DEPENDABLE POLICE FOR A PEACEFUL NATION

120
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,800
It's not just skill.

121
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:19,960
The bullet isn't ordinary, either.

122
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:23,320
It looks specially made.

123
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:25,880
More recoil than standard ammunition.

124
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,880
Designed specifically
for long-range shooting.

125
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:31,200
Where did he get it?

126
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:35,640
Not many people can make this stuff.

127
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:38,920
We need to find Gun and Methee's hideout.

128
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:42,840
And also the guy who made this bullet.

129
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:02,080
Hey. Wait, wait. Gun.

130
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:04,640
-We need to talk.
-About what?

131
00:19:09,040 --> 00:19:11,680
Are you sure about
letting Rada stay with you?

132
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:14,600
You don't trust her?

133
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:18,280
It's not that.

134
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:23,840
I've seen a lot of people
ruined by those close to them.

135
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:27,000
I had no choice.

136
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:31,480
No, you made a choice.

137
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:36,480
It's because she never left me.

138
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,800
You're being too paranoid.

139
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:41,960
I'm not paranoid.

140
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:45,720
The day she went to buy you medicine,

141
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,880
she knew I was following her
from the start.

142
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:54,960
Normal people don't listen
for footsteps when being followed.

143
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:26,000
Oh, Methee?

144
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:35,520
<i>Rada was unusually alert and cautious.</i>

145
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:42,800
I told her myself
to be careful when going out.

146
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,280
But

147
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:48,960
a normal person
wouldn't notice that fast, man.

148
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:51,120
-Look, she--
-What are you talking about?

149
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:57,920
Nothing. I was about to head up.

150
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:00,480
Where did you go?

151
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:04,560
I bought some food for you guys.

152
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:10,120
Hey, you're bleeding again.

153
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:14,840
Be careful. The wound hasn't healed yet.
Let's go upstairs. I'll dress your wound.

154
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:21,400
Go ahead. I'll find
something to eat myself. See you.

155
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:51,400
Don't move so much. The wound
isn't fully closed. It'll get infected.

156
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:03,160
Am I making you uncomfortable?

157
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:09,440
Can I still trust you?

158
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,560
Then look at my actions.

159
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:19,880
I know you've got important things to do.

160
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:24,240
If I ever make you uncomfortable,

161
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:27,120
you can tell me to leave.

162
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:31,040
I promise I'll go far away

163
00:22:31,120 --> 00:22:33,040
and won't cause you trouble.

164
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:42,200
You're going to abandon your patient?

165
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:45,720
That's pretty mean coming from a nurse.

166
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:58,720
I need you.

167
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:06,480
We are family.

168
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:18,080
I understand your vengeance.

169
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,960
But you're becoming a criminal.

170
00:23:24,560 --> 00:23:26,040
I'd rather be a bad guy

171
00:23:27,320 --> 00:23:31,600
than let them keep scamming
and hurting countless people.

172
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:36,520
I used to believe in ideals,

173
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:39,840
but now I know I can't survive on them.

174
00:23:40,880 --> 00:23:42,360
This world is getting worse.

175
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:48,120
Corrupt people are in charge,
using the law to enrich themselves.

176
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:54,000
If I keep working in the system,
I'm just serving them.

177
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:58,320
There's only one way.

178
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:03,920
I have to step out and demand justice.

179
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:05,720
But your grandma wouldn't be happy

180
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:08,080
if she had known
you were throwing your life away.

181
00:24:13,600 --> 00:24:16,320
I believe if she'd known the whole truth,

182
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:18,800
she'd beg you to stop.

183
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:22,960
She'd beg you to live your life.

184
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:27,080
Just like I'm begging you.

185
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:42,000
You are my dream.

186
00:24:43,680 --> 00:24:45,640
I want to spend my life with you.

187
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:49,440
I don't want to lose you.

188
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:31,080
Here.

189
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:32,240
DEPENDABLE POLICE FOR A PEACEFUL NATION

190
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:33,560
This guy Paed.

191
00:25:34,280 --> 00:25:36,480
He makes and sells
black-market guns and ammo.

192
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:40,960
With a face like that?

193
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:45,800
Don't judge by appearances.
He served time in prison.

194
00:25:46,600 --> 00:25:48,720
He picked up both skills
and connections in prison.

195
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:52,720
So, what does he have to do with Gun?

196
00:25:52,800 --> 00:25:56,800
When he was in prison,
Gun helped his parents.

197
00:25:57,320 --> 00:25:59,360
When he got out, he returned the favor.

198
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:05,320
-Find him fast.
-Yes, sir.

199
00:26:19,960 --> 00:26:21,160
Gun, it's me.

200
00:26:28,360 --> 00:26:29,360
Gun.

201
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:36,640
Step outside with me. Let's go.

202
00:26:38,600 --> 00:26:40,280
What is it? Just talk here.

203
00:26:43,720 --> 00:26:45,280
Sarawut knows about Paed.

204
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:53,240
Hey, I have to go help my friend.

205
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:56,240
Wait here. I'll be right back.

206
00:26:59,040 --> 00:27:00,680
I'll make things real

207
00:27:02,080 --> 00:27:03,560
between us.

208
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:25,800
It's not time for the drop yet.

209
00:27:28,440 --> 00:27:29,680
You don't listen, do you?

210
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:40,520
Ouch!

211
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:43,240
-Where is Gun?
-Ugh.

212
00:27:43,320 --> 00:27:44,840
I don't know!

213
00:27:48,240 --> 00:27:49,200
What about Methee?

214
00:27:49,280 --> 00:27:51,120
I don't know. I said I don't know!

215
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:53,360
You don't know?

216
00:27:59,640 --> 00:28:01,160
You make bullets for them, don't you?

217
00:28:01,240 --> 00:28:02,480
I didn't!

218
00:28:03,760 --> 00:28:04,680
You didn't?

219
00:28:06,760 --> 00:28:07,880
Then you're useless.

220
00:28:15,120 --> 00:28:15,960
Paed, run!

221
00:28:34,040 --> 00:28:34,920
Hey!

222
00:28:52,840 --> 00:28:53,960
Gun!

223
00:28:56,760 --> 00:28:57,800
Go, Paed!

224
00:28:59,840 --> 00:29:01,280
Hurry. Go, go!

225
00:29:03,360 --> 00:29:04,600
Run!

226
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:21,800
Paed.

227
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:23,600
WINNER TEXTILES

228
00:29:28,320 --> 00:29:29,200
Paed, wake up. Paed.

229
00:29:29,880 --> 00:29:31,040
Paed!

230
00:29:42,360 --> 00:29:44,240
Paed, can you hear me? Paed!

231
00:29:44,920 --> 00:29:48,200
Gun, let's go. He's dead. Go!

232
00:29:54,200 --> 00:29:55,120
-Boss.
-Thun!

233
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:56,440
Boss.

234
00:29:58,240 --> 00:29:59,240
Oh.

235
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:19,640
-Boss.
-Hm?

236
00:30:21,120 --> 00:30:22,360
Gun survived.

237
00:30:29,480 --> 00:30:30,880
If he survives…

238
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:36,120
I'll have to play my last card.

239
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:11,400
How did Seehan's guys know Paed's address?

240
00:31:14,480 --> 00:31:15,800
Did you tell Rada?

241
00:31:20,520 --> 00:31:22,160
You suspect her?

242
00:31:27,080 --> 00:31:28,480
I don't trust her.

243
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:32,880
I never told Rada about this.

244
00:31:38,360 --> 00:31:41,760
Then, I'll investigate

245
00:31:41,840 --> 00:31:43,240
how they found out.

246
00:32:11,600 --> 00:32:12,920
Rada?

247
00:32:14,480 --> 00:32:17,120
Rada.

248
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:18,880
Hey. I'm here.

249
00:32:30,840 --> 00:32:32,200
You're okay, right?

250
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:35,320
I was worried about you.

251
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:38,640
We have to get out of here.

252
00:32:39,400 --> 00:32:41,920
-Where are we going?
-Somewhere safe.

253
00:32:42,920 --> 00:32:44,360
Pack only what's necessary.

254
00:32:51,040 --> 00:32:52,440
Paisan is dead.

255
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:54,920
Decha is dead.

256
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:57,880
I won't be an easy target for him.

257
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:03,400
Bring me his corpse.

258
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:13,120
-Ready?
-Wait, wait.

259
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:14,920
Let me take the cactus too.

260
00:34:03,960 --> 00:34:04,920
Hey.

261
00:34:10,639 --> 00:34:13,719
Who dies first? You or her?

262
00:34:17,639 --> 00:34:19,719
Let her go.
She has nothing to do with this.

263
00:34:20,480 --> 00:34:22,320
You must really love this woman.

264
00:34:25,440 --> 00:34:28,000
Don't. I said let her go.

265
00:34:28,080 --> 00:34:29,239
Such a gentleman.

266
00:34:29,880 --> 00:34:33,400
I won't let you be a hero. I'll kill her

267
00:34:36,199 --> 00:34:38,120
and make you live with the guilt forever.

268
00:34:40,840 --> 00:34:42,040
No!

269
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:07,840
Who are you?

270
00:35:13,600 --> 00:35:14,920
Who do you work for?

271
00:35:18,280 --> 00:35:19,280
Sirin?

272
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:28,360
Seehan?

273
00:35:30,720 --> 00:35:33,880
Seehan is my adopted father.

274
00:35:37,920 --> 00:35:39,680
Was anything you told me…

275
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:42,520
even true?

276
00:35:48,240 --> 00:35:50,000
My parents really died.

277
00:35:51,160 --> 00:35:55,480
I really was an orphan,
sent to an orphanage.

278
00:35:56,080 --> 00:35:58,160
No one wants a child who's a burden.

279
00:35:59,480 --> 00:36:01,400
The only thing I kept from you

280
00:36:03,120 --> 00:36:05,720
was that I'm Seehan's adopted daughter,

281
00:36:07,520 --> 00:36:11,640
and he made me Rada.

282
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:24,440
So our meeting…

283
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:28,280
was no coincidence.

284
00:36:42,320 --> 00:36:43,320
Hey!

285
00:36:49,560 --> 00:36:50,920
You risked your life,

286
00:36:52,480 --> 00:36:53,760
just to make me trust you.

287
00:36:55,200 --> 00:36:57,480
I was sent to get close to you.

288
00:36:58,160 --> 00:36:59,160
Oh.

289
00:37:01,240 --> 00:37:02,120
Come on.

290
00:37:04,560 --> 00:37:05,920
You!

291
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:07,120
Hey!

292
00:37:07,920 --> 00:37:09,080
You'll hit Miss Rada.

293
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:12,840
-She's not involved.
-Orders are orders.

294
00:37:13,440 --> 00:37:14,480
Then try me.

295
00:37:35,240 --> 00:37:36,480
And you did everything…

296
00:37:39,160 --> 00:37:40,440
to make me trust you.

297
00:38:05,040 --> 00:38:06,600
Methee warned me.

298
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:12,680
But I chose…

299
00:38:15,040 --> 00:38:16,360
to trust you.

300
00:38:19,840 --> 00:38:23,160
You know all the bad things Seehan did.

301
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:24,640
Why stay by his side?

302
00:38:24,720 --> 00:38:25,920
I have no choice.

303
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:27,800
Everyone always says that.

304
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:29,600
You'll never understand me.

305
00:38:30,600 --> 00:38:33,280
Without him, I might
have died a long time ago.

306
00:38:36,840 --> 00:38:38,800
He might be evil in other people's eyes,

307
00:38:39,840 --> 00:38:41,800
but he was never cruel to me.

308
00:38:43,280 --> 00:38:44,720
Because someone like me

309
00:38:45,640 --> 00:38:47,960
never had a choice to begin with.

310
00:38:54,000 --> 00:38:55,760
What about your feelings for me?

311
00:38:59,080 --> 00:39:00,440
Was any of that real?

312
00:39:12,760 --> 00:39:15,240
-It doesn't matter to me any--
-But it matters to me.

313
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:21,520
Or was it all in my head?

314
00:39:49,280 --> 00:39:52,000
I'd gladly give up everything,

315
00:39:52,080 --> 00:39:54,120
but you must kill him.

316
00:39:54,200 --> 00:39:58,200
Seehan wouldn't take in
an orphan for nothing.

317
00:39:58,280 --> 00:39:59,600
There has to be a reason.

318
00:39:59,680 --> 00:40:01,680
You still trust that treacherous woman?

319
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:04,200
I know I was played, but I know deep down

320
00:40:04,280 --> 00:40:05,560
Rada isn't like that.

321
00:40:06,640 --> 00:40:07,720
-Hey, duck!
-Hey!

322
00:40:07,800 --> 00:40:08,880
Hurry!

323
00:40:21,160 --> 00:40:22,640
Bam. Kick him away.

324
00:40:22,720 --> 00:40:24,640
-Go. Bam!
-Pin him down.

325
00:40:24,720 --> 00:40:27,080
-Bam! Bam! Nice, Mik.
-What now?

326
00:40:27,160 --> 00:40:28,440
Bam!

327
00:40:28,520 --> 00:40:30,280
-Bang!
-Shoot. Bang, bang!

328
00:40:30,360 --> 00:40:31,560
Bang, bang, bang!

329
00:40:31,640 --> 00:40:33,640
-Hey! Bang, bang, bang!
-Bang, bang, bang!

330
00:40:33,720 --> 00:40:36,280
Come here. Stay right here first.

331
00:40:36,360 --> 00:40:39,080
-Bang, bang!
-Bang, bang, bang! Go, go!

332
00:40:40,400 --> 00:40:42,400
-Bang, bang, bang!
-Bang, bang! Go fast.

333
00:40:42,480 --> 00:40:44,080
I'll jump over.

334
00:40:44,160 --> 00:40:45,640
Bang, bang, bang!

335
00:40:45,720 --> 00:40:47,440
Three, four.

336
00:40:47,520 --> 00:40:49,840
-Take cover.
-Bang, bang, bang!

337
00:40:49,920 --> 00:40:51,960
-One, two, three, out!
-Bang!

338
00:40:53,040 --> 00:40:55,480
-Cut. Cut.
-Methee. Start over.

339
00:40:55,560 --> 00:40:58,440
-Shoot. Wait, Methee. Redo the entrance.
-Bang, bang!

340
00:40:58,520 --> 00:40:59,840
The shot will be right here.

341
00:40:59,920 --> 00:41:01,440
-Over there.
-There?

342
00:41:01,520 --> 00:41:04,080
-When I say so, Methee shoots.
-Bang!

343
00:41:04,160 --> 00:41:06,840
-Bang, bang!
-Shoot that way.

344
00:41:23,160 --> 00:41:25,680
Boss! Boss.

345
00:41:59,120 --> 00:42:01,480
Subtitle translation by: Anan Pratchayakul
